  "designMd": {
    "raw": "---\nname: Arc’IT AI — build on what works\nversion: 3.0.0\n---\n\n# Direction and scope\n\n21 September 2026. Gustav wants a calmer landing page about his expertise and practical delivery: review what a customer has already built, improve its security and foundations, and establish a useful way to continue the work. The selected deliverable is an editable, saved OpenPencil design, plus English copy and a repository research issue. No live page, Worker, AIOS, Notion, sibling project or dependency changes. Preserve R1, R2 and the optional dashboard concept.\n\n## Baseline and requested changes\n\nR2.1 provides the green landscape identity, Geist family, original Cut Six hero logo, VSL-first rhythm and business-first responsibility. Retain those. Remove the pictorial offer icons, “Prototype to Production” and “AI Agent Factories” as front-page offer names, and the entire “Two systems / One delivery process” section. The earlier mascot is not reintroduced.\n\nUse only the wordmark in the header; the actual mark stays centred in the hero. Footer has external links only and “Business first. Security built in.” instead of the rejected slogan. A small optional example link can sit under the third offer; no large dashboard sales section or proprietary-platform claim.\n\n## Reference adaptation\n\n1. **Arc’IT R2.1**: [previous direction](../secure-agents-r2-2026-09-14/DESIGN.md), actual local panorama and Cut Six geometry. Highest visual precedence after the owner’s corrections. Reuse existing owned assets; no brand redesign.\n2. **Kastanje, “Landing page redesign”**, task `01a0ab4c-458d-7f51-9893-a1e3e33ea4c1`. [Live reference](https://kastanje-demo.gustavonline.workers.dev/), inspected at 1440×1000 and 390×844. Transfer the full-bleed scene, header over the scene, restrained translucent navigation and mobile separation of copy and scenery. Do not transfer the chestnut, orange palette, pricing, product UI or customer claims. Arc’IT retains a centred desktop hero because the owner specifically wants its logo in the middle; this intentionally differs from Kastanje’s left-aligned headline.\n3. **[Agentic Engineer](https://agentic-engineer.ai/)**, live offers inspected 21 September. Transfer the small abstract moving marks, generous negative space and direct offer grouping. Create original green point/ring/line studies; no shields, gears, code windows, literal consulting icons or copied motion code. Do not inherit its pricing, scarcity or proprietary-platform claims.\n\nThe reference screenshots remain task proof in `output/playwright/`, not design assets or customer-facing images. “Codex Fred” was clarified as the Kastanje task, not another website.\n\n## Page composition\n\nOne desktop frame at 1440 px and one narrow layout at 390 px, both with editable text and shapes. A neighbouring notes/motion frame explains links, planned motion and the static design boundary. Native source is the durable artifact; an editor server is only a way to open it.\n\nDesktop: header over panorama → centred logo/headline/CTA → founder video → three airy offer columns → inquiry and practical questions → green landscape footer. No factory loop between offers and inquiry. Reading shell 1160–1200 px, generous section gaps and fine rules rather than nested cards. Use green to interrupt the warm reading surface, not black/beige throughout.\n\nMobile: wordmark and one primary action; readable copy on warm paper before a shorter panorama strip. The hero mark remains centred above the text. Stack the three offers; keep their abstract marks small. Inquiry uses one column. Footer external links may wrap. Do not shrink body copy or omit qualifications to fit.\n\n## Identity and tokens\n\nPaper `#f8f2e8`, cream `#fffaf1`, ink `#18211d`, muted `#615f56`, deep green `#14211d`, action green `#236b59`, pale sage `#b9d9c8`. Warm-white text over a darkened desktop panorama; strong dark text on mobile paper. Green buttons with warm-white text in reading sections. At least 16 px body on mobile, 17–18 px desktop; restrained mono labels no smaller than 11–12 px in the design. Contrast and spacing must be inspected in the actual native canvas.\n\nGeist Pixel for the wordmark and primary headings, Geist Sans for prose, Geist Mono for labels. Use the real Cut Six geometry in the hero; no eyes, shadow, limbs or perpetual character motion. The landscape is the existing `public/assets/arcitai-panorama-day-v1.jpg`, not new AI-generated artwork. Its illustration remains raster; text, controls, logo geometry and abstract motifs remain editable.\n\n## Abstract graphics and motion intent\n\nThree original compositions: scattered points gathering into a quiet centre; offset rings finding alignment; a paced line of short strokes with one advancing accent. They suggest focus, examination and continuity without literal icons or an architectural diagram. The native document shows a still state and separate motion notes. Do not claim that OpenPencil demonstrates working web animation.\n\nFor later web implementation: slow, restrained movement; no auto-changing text; pause on reduced motion and offscreen/hidden state; a static first state remains complete. The hero logo may keep its one-time assembly from R2.1. No canvas animation framework or additional runtime is authorised by this design.\n\n## Copy, actions and honesty\n\n[Website copy](../../content/practical-delivery-r3-2026-09-21/website-copy.md) owns the English editorial handoff. Header, hero, VSL, offers and inquiry point toward a conversation about the existing setup. Native drawings of controls are not working website controls. The VSL is unrecorded. The inquiry sends nothing. Any later web implementation must preserve the existing Worker contract and form behavior, including accessible errors and focus.\n\nThe optional example link maps to the [preserved dashboard concept](../agent-factories-r1-2026-09-14/index.html), with sample-data/template labels. It is not an installed product or published open-source package. A later template decision is captured in [issue #6](https://github.com/arcitai/arcitai/issues/6); no new repository or licence is selected here.\n\n## Review and limits\n\nSame-task technical/editorial/native review by Codex; Gustav’s final copy/design choice remains pending. Inspect native desktop/mobile frames and notes, actual editable nodes, File → Save, persisted bytes, source preservation, and a reopen of the saved candidate. Verify fonts and embedded scene separately. Native exports must be visually inspected; disclose any native font-export limitation rather than presenting fallback typography as accepted.\n\n- **Known limitations:** Static editable design, not a responsive website implementation, working animation, recorded VSL, sent inquiry, security audit or running factory. The exact lost Chrome variant was not located; earlier files and snapshots are preserved. The reused OpenPencil 0.8.4 runtime has historical verified-release provenance from the prior Kastanje workbench; this session checks its version/layout and records current binary hashes, not a fresh VSIX download verification.\n",
    "projectName": "Direction and scope",
    "colorPalette": [
      {
        "name": "Paper `",
        "hex": "#F8F2E8",
        "role": "`, cream `#fffaf1`, ink `#18211d`, muted `#615f56`, deep green `#14211d`, action green `#236b59`, pale sage `#b9d9c8`. Warm-white text over a darkened desktop panorama; strong dark text on mobile paper. Green buttons with warm-white text in reading sections. At least 16 px body on mobile, 17–18 px desktop; restrained mono labels no smaller than 11–12 px in the design. Contrast and spacing must be inspected in the actual native canvas."
      }
    ],
